WEBVTT

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:07.060
Wow!

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:09.190
What a beautiful city!

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:12.360
It's just as lively as the capital!

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:14.500
Indeed it is. Indeed it is.

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:17.520
This is our city, Amroth.

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:21.230
Mile! You're being embarrassing! 
Stop sitting like that.

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:25.210
Amroth is a much bigger city 
than I thought it'd be.

00:00:25.330 --> 00:00:27.020
It makes sense.

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:31.630
After all, it is a merchant city 
on the border of the Albarn Empire.

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:35.220
Kingdom of Brandel

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:35.220
Royal Capital

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:35.340
Amroth

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:35.340
Albarn Empire

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:50.230
Royal Capital

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:59.490
Kingdom of Tils

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:35.560
It's "Nano-chan's Explanation Corner"!

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:50.230
Amroth

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:39.280
This is where Mile-sama and the others, 
the Crimson Vow, registered as Hunters.

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:40.490
The Kingdom of Tils.

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:43.880
And this is where they 
are now, the city of Amroth.

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:44.600
See?

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:47.400
The neighboring Albarn Empire is very close,

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.980
so trade and cultural exchange
 between the two is vigorous.

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:56.990
Albarn Empire

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:57.240
Royal Capital

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:59.240
Kingdom of Brandel

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:52.560
To continue the explanation...

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:57.220
Over here we have the Kingdom of Brandel, where
 Mile-sama was forced to flee in the night.

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:59.370
Royal Capital

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:59.370
Amroth

00:00:57.220 --> 00:00:59.480
Oh! Apologies for the digression.

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:03.270
Amroth is a city that trades 
heavily with the Albarn Empire!

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:05.210
This has been "Nano-chan's Explanation Corner"!

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:09.660
That's why being able to successfully 
transport merchants' goods

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:12.380
is a matter of life and death.

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:16.170
The fact that we made it here 
safely with the merchandise

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:20.600
is all thanks to you getting 
rid of those bandits.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:22.680
Thank you, truly.

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:25.790
O-Oh, no. There's no need to bow to us.

00:01:25.790 --> 00:01:29.980
Fulfilling the requests of our 
clients is our job as Hunters.

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:33.010
That's right! We don't need thanks!

00:01:33.010 --> 00:01:34.190
After all...

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:37.200
We never fail.

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:42.790
I'm sorry! I went too far...

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:48.040
As cheerful a young lady as ever!

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:51.880
Were you imitating a popular play 
or something from the capital?

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:54.130
I'd like to see it, too.

00:01:55.640 --> 00:01:57.280
Grandpa!

00:01:57.880 --> 00:02:02.510
Oh! Looks like my granddaughter's 
come to greet me!

00:02:04.010 --> 00:02:04.840
Huh?

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:05.890
Where is she?

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:09.800
He said we reminded him of 
his granddaughter, right?

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:12.650
He said Pauline-san looked 
like her too, but...

00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:15.600
Welcome home, Grandpa!

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:17.900
Yes, I just came back.

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:20.240
Were you a good girl?

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:21.060
Yeah!

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:22.430
I'm a good girl!

00:02:22.430 --> 00:02:24.080
I see. Is that so?

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:26.140
There, there. Good girl.

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:28.770
Good girl.

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:32.230
My granddaughter, Anne. What do you think?

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:35.070
She's cute, just like you. Right?

00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:36.300
Hello!

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:38.850
Y-Yes, she is.

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:41.300
<i>She's still a little girl!</i>

00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:15.980
Didn't I Say to Make My Abilities 
Average in the Next Life?!

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:20.990
<b>Episode 6</b>

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:20.990
<b>Didn't I Say I'm Not Going Into the Forest Anymore?!</b>

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:23.990
Anne-chan still likes having 
people dote on her, doesn't she?

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:28.610
Well, her parents were both called 
to other towns on urgent business.

00:04:28.610 --> 00:04:30.120
Were you lonely?

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:31.860
I'm not lonely!

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:38.700
Hey. Since you're here, would you
 like me to show you around?

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:40.340
You wouldn't mind?

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:42.820
All the goods have been delivered.

00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:45.680
It's the least I can do as thanks.

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:48.470
I want you to enjoy our city to the fullest.

00:04:48.740 --> 00:04:51.710
But we have to get back to the capital.

00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:54.020
There's no need for us to rush back, right?

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:56.940
After completing a job, 
a little break is a good thing.

00:04:57.180 --> 00:04:59.370
It's okay, isn't it, Onee-chan?

00:04:59.370 --> 00:04:59.930
Huh?

00:05:00.450 --> 00:05:03.490
I-If you insist, I suppose we can't refuse.

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:07.070
Everyone sightseeing together
 and buying snacks...

00:05:07.070 --> 00:05:08.990
Could it be that this is...

00:05:10.060 --> 00:05:12.300
Come on! Eat up! Have some deer crackers!

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:14.000
Famous
Deer Crackers

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:14.000
They're so cute!

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:16.460
It feels like a class trip!

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:18.200
Class trip?

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:19.270
What's that?

00:05:19.270 --> 00:05:21.500
Oh! Uh... it's a secret family technique!

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:23.950
Oh! There you are!

00:05:23.950 --> 00:05:25.290
Old-timer!

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:26.010
Huh?

00:05:27.540 --> 00:05:28.870
Sorry about this.

00:05:28.870 --> 00:05:31.010
This job came in suddenly.

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:34.080
Not at all. It's good to be busy.

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:35.770
That's true...

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:41.020
Just when I thought I'd be able to 
go on a class trip with everyone.

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:44.530
Grandpa! Here! For you!

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:45.900
What's this?

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:49.320
I bought it to protect you, Grandpa!

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:52.280
I see, I see! Thank you!

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:55.980
There, there! Good girl!

00:05:55.980 --> 00:05:58.500
You're just so cute!

00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:07.590
I'll be back!

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:10.720
Have a safe trip, Grandpa!

00:06:13.350 --> 00:06:14.990
Well, he's left.

00:06:14.990 --> 00:06:16.080
Yes, he has.

00:06:17.690 --> 00:06:20.860
Now, it's time for us to get going, too.

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:23.540
We may not have Grandpa to show us around,

00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:25.360
but I haven't given up!

00:06:25.580 --> 00:06:27.320
A class trip!

00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:29.080
What is that, anyway?

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:30.760
Don't worry about it.

00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:34.040
Oh! There's a recommended street 
full of food stalls that way.

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:35.870
First, we eat!

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:38.710
Then the first sightseeing 
spot we'll go to is...

00:06:38.710 --> 00:06:41.750
The one closest to the street stalls is...

00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:43.980
Oh! There aren't any deer in this city!

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:20.320
We have to make sure to buy souvenirs.

00:07:20.320 --> 00:07:23.070
And since they don't really 
know what a class trip is,

00:07:23.070 --> 00:07:25.230
I'll have to pick some out for them!

00:07:25.230 --> 00:07:27.920
I'll buy something to take 
back for Lenny-chan, too!

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:30.800
Oh! Th-Those are...!

00:07:31.030 --> 00:07:34.790
Pennants! Carved bears! Wooden swords!

00:07:34.790 --> 00:07:37.060
They have these in this world, too!

00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:40.920
Somehow, I get the feeling that 
if you give those as presents,

00:07:40.920 --> 00:07:42.100
they won't make the recipient happy.

00:07:42.100 --> 00:07:43.560
What are you talking about?

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:45.980
When you think of destination souvenirs,
 you think of these, right?

00:07:46.280 --> 00:07:50.440
See? In commemoration of our trip,
 we have matching ones!

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:51.990
Aren't they cute?

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:55.020
Bear! Bear! Bear!

00:07:55.020 --> 00:07:58.120
I think I'll get a wooden 
sword for Lenny-chan.

00:07:58.120 --> 00:08:00.800
You can put pennants up on the walls, you know?

00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:03.270
Every time we go to a new town,
 we can buy another one.

00:08:03.270 --> 00:08:05.800
We can fill the room with them!

00:08:05.800 --> 00:08:07.170
Mile-chan...

00:08:09.750 --> 00:08:11.780
Yes, ma'am! "We can't waste money!"

00:08:11.780 --> 00:08:13.520
"Return them immediately!"

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:14.430
Right?

00:08:21.070 --> 00:08:22.390
You know...

00:08:22.550 --> 00:08:24.560
All of these seem pretty expensive.

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:26.770
And some things are sold out.

00:08:27.030 --> 00:08:28.540
They can't help it.

00:08:28.540 --> 00:08:33.120
Since the wagons carrying the merchandise 
are getting attacked by bandits,

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:35.660
they can't get in new stock 
the way they'd like to.

00:08:36.040 --> 00:08:37.030
I see.

00:08:37.030 --> 00:08:39.540
But that situation should 
be getting better now.

00:08:40.070 --> 00:08:43.980
After all, we got rid of those bandits, right?

00:08:44.470 --> 00:08:45.960
Terrible news!

00:08:46.340 --> 00:08:46.980
Huh?

00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:50.680
The wagons have been 
attacked by bandits again!

00:08:50.680 --> 00:08:51.210
What?

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:53.590
They said there's hardly anyone left alive!

00:08:56.070 --> 00:08:57.260
Reina-san!

00:09:01.150 --> 00:09:03.270
Damn it. They really got us.

00:09:03.460 --> 00:09:04.960
Those bandits.

00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:07.830
There were so many of them. 
They were waiting there to ambush us!

00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:14.780
<i>How terrible.</i>

00:09:18.650 --> 00:09:20.690
So, how are the others?

00:09:20.690 --> 00:09:22.190
W-Well...

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:24.900
It took everything I had 
just to get away, so I...

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:29.510
I can't imagine that any others survived.

00:09:29.510 --> 00:09:31.120
Everyone slaughtered...

00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:32.420
Blast it!

00:09:32.680 --> 00:09:34.680
It... It can't be...

00:09:37.190 --> 00:09:38.190
Grandpa...

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:42.090
What about Grandpa?

00:09:42.760 --> 00:09:44.560
He's not coming back?

00:09:47.740 --> 00:09:48.820
No!

00:09:49.350 --> 00:09:50.800
Grandpa!

00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:53.320
Grandpa!

00:09:55.520 --> 00:09:57.700
It's all right. It's all right!

00:09:59.850 --> 00:10:01.200
Anne-chan...

00:10:14.410 --> 00:10:17.410
There were others besides the ones 
we got rid of, weren't there?

00:10:17.950 --> 00:10:21.390
Inhuman bands of bandits 
who make everyone suffer.

00:10:21.730 --> 00:10:22.730
Yes.

00:10:22.730 --> 00:10:25.640
I'm embarrassed for getting so excited 
when I didn't really understand anything.

00:10:26.030 --> 00:10:29.020
That aside... Reina is taking a long time.

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:36.940
She said she'd come straight 
here after taking Anne home.

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:38.910
She couldn't have!

00:10:39.370 --> 00:10:40.360
Reina-san!

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:48.250
As long as there's breath in 
my body, I won't let you die.

00:10:48.650 --> 00:10:50.210
<i>I promised him.</i>

00:10:50.690 --> 00:10:52.490
<i>I said I wouldn't let him die!</i>

00:10:53.350 --> 00:10:54.460
<i>And now...</i>

00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:10.990
<i>Reina-san!</i>

00:11:19.770 --> 00:11:21.920
<i>I'm sorry, everyone. I just...</i>

00:11:21.920 --> 00:11:23.510
<i>I can't forgive them!</i>

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:25.620
Everything all right over here?

00:11:26.840 --> 00:11:28.780
Don't let down your guard
just because it's night.

00:11:28.780 --> 00:11:33.080
We can't allow any goods connected 
with Amroth to pass through.

00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:33.630
Yes, sir!

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:37.040
You know, the raid today was too easy.

00:11:37.040 --> 00:11:39.350
There wasn't a single decent 
Hunter guarding them.

00:11:39.350 --> 00:11:42.130
Being bandits isn't such a bad job after all.

00:11:45.930 --> 00:11:47.010
Who are you?

00:11:47.280 --> 00:11:48.530
Was it you?

00:11:48.530 --> 00:11:51.020
Were you the ones who attacked 
the merchants from Amroth?

00:11:51.020 --> 00:11:52.390
Attacked that old man?

00:11:52.620 --> 00:11:54.900
You! A Hunter from Amroth, are you?

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:02.900
Roar, flames! Into a ball of fire!

00:12:03.290 --> 00:12:04.440
A mage!

00:12:04.440 --> 00:12:06.240
O water! Become ice!

00:12:06.820 --> 00:12:08.910
Fireball!

00:12:11.070 --> 00:12:12.870
Fireball, continuous fire!

00:12:15.370 --> 00:12:17.880
We have mages, too.

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:19.890
Contact the main force now!

00:12:19.890 --> 00:12:20.500
Yes, sir!

00:12:21.260 --> 00:12:22.550
You're not getting away!

00:12:22.550 --> 00:12:23.760
Icicle.

00:12:29.920 --> 00:12:31.130
Sorry about this,

00:12:31.130 --> 00:12:32.390
but since you heard us...

00:12:32.690 --> 00:12:35.020
You may be a child, but you'll have to die!

00:12:41.090 --> 00:12:41.980
What's this?

00:12:45.330 --> 00:12:47.030
G-Guys...

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:49.200
Are you all right, Reina-san?

00:12:49.560 --> 00:12:50.950
Who are all of you?

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:53.050
We should be asking who you are.

00:12:53.050 --> 00:12:55.080
Don't you lay a hand on our friend!

00:12:55.590 --> 00:12:57.420
Please, get a hold of yourself.

00:12:57.420 --> 00:12:58.740
Enemies? Where are they?

00:12:59.360 --> 00:13:01.490
From the voices... there's a lot of them.

00:13:01.920 --> 00:13:03.340
Let's retreat for now.

00:13:03.620 --> 00:13:04.520
No!

00:13:05.480 --> 00:13:07.050
The injured should keep quiet.

00:13:07.400 --> 00:13:08.310
Mile!

00:13:08.310 --> 00:13:09.300
Got it!

00:13:10.940 --> 00:13:12.030
In that case...

00:13:12.030 --> 00:13:12.810
Poof!

00:13:15.460 --> 00:13:16.850
A smoke screen, huh?

00:13:20.890 --> 00:13:21.870
Ow, ow, ow!

00:13:21.870 --> 00:13:24.360
See? Behave yourself.

00:13:24.360 --> 00:13:27.970
If you don't hold still, I won't 
be able to heal what can be healed.

00:13:27.970 --> 00:13:29.830
Why did all of you come here?

00:13:30.040 --> 00:13:32.530
Why? Isn't it obvious?

00:13:32.530 --> 00:13:34.580
We couldn't believe you'd 
charge off by yourself.

00:13:37.340 --> 00:13:40.480
I know you probably didn't 
want to get us involved,

00:13:40.480 --> 00:13:42.840
but there's no need to hold us 
at arm's length, Reina-san.

00:13:43.860 --> 00:13:46.620
I know trying to take revenge is stupid.

00:13:47.010 --> 00:13:51.060
But when I saw Anne crying, 
I just couldn't forgive them!

00:13:51.500 --> 00:13:54.720
Those people who stole that 
little girl's family from her!

00:13:55.080 --> 00:13:57.060
Still. Going of one your own—

00:13:57.060 --> 00:13:58.730
This is my problem!

00:13:59.040 --> 00:14:00.520
Just leave me alone!

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:01.770
It's got nothing to do with y—

00:14:14.960 --> 00:14:16.870
Reina-san, you're the world's biggest idiot!

00:14:16.870 --> 00:14:17.620
Huh?

00:14:17.970 --> 00:14:19.890
If not an idiot, then foolish!

00:14:19.890 --> 00:14:21.930
A moronic nincompoop!

00:14:21.930 --> 00:14:23.880
You clueless eggplant's calyx!

00:14:24.150 --> 00:14:27.380
Wh-Wha? I don't have any 
idea what you're saying.

00:14:27.810 --> 00:14:29.700
Reina-san, it was you who said it!

00:14:29.700 --> 00:14:32.960
You couldn't stand losing your family again!

00:14:32.960 --> 00:14:34.760
Th-That's...

00:14:34.760 --> 00:14:39.390
Then if we lost our dear 
friend, lost our family...

00:14:39.840 --> 00:14:42.150
You think we wouldn't be sad?

00:14:44.360 --> 00:14:45.330
Mile...

00:14:47.800 --> 00:14:49.740
You're not the only one, Reina,

00:14:50.130 --> 00:14:53.140
who doesn't want to lose their precious family.

00:14:53.140 --> 00:14:55.900
Honestly, you don't even understand that?

00:14:55.900 --> 00:14:58.410
You're the world's biggest idiot,
 just like Mile said.

00:15:09.670 --> 00:15:10.580
Guys...

00:15:21.800 --> 00:15:26.220
Oops! I forgot to cast a search spell again!

00:15:26.620 --> 00:15:28.230
We expect that now.

00:15:28.230 --> 00:15:31.040
Greetings, unknown Hunters!

00:15:31.040 --> 00:15:32.920
We are bandits!

00:15:32.920 --> 00:15:35.200
Drop your weapons and surrender quietly.

00:15:35.520 --> 00:15:38.340
"We are bandits"? "Surrender"?

00:15:38.340 --> 00:15:41.200
Somehow, those don't sound like 
things bandits would say.

00:15:41.200 --> 00:15:43.540
Plus, the way they move 
like they're under orders,

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:45.210
and the uniformity of their equipment...

00:15:45.600 --> 00:15:47.340
These are some suspicious "bandits."

00:15:48.770 --> 00:15:50.380
You're soldiers, aren't you?

00:15:51.250 --> 00:15:52.730
What are you saying?

00:15:52.730 --> 00:15:55.220
We are clearly a fully-fledged bandit group!

00:15:55.220 --> 00:15:58.140
Why would soldiers 
pretend to be bandits, anyway?

00:15:58.580 --> 00:16:00.810
Could it be... trade disruption?

00:16:02.600 --> 00:16:06.060
If, for example, 
the Albarn Empire resented Amroth

00:16:06.060 --> 00:16:09.080
for gaining more from foreign 
trade than they did,

00:16:09.080 --> 00:16:12.070
so they dressed up as bandits 
to attack the caravans...

00:16:12.840 --> 00:16:13.570
Something like that?

00:16:15.620 --> 00:16:16.920
Bull's-eye, huh?

00:16:16.920 --> 00:16:18.200
Seems like it.

00:16:18.440 --> 00:16:19.590
Indeed!

00:16:19.590 --> 00:16:23.710
We are the elite corps of the proud 
Albarn Empire's military forces.

00:16:23.980 --> 00:16:27.520
Then those bandits before 
were just small fry.

00:16:27.520 --> 00:16:29.210
But why would a military...

00:16:29.650 --> 00:16:32.840
Why did you slaughter innocent people?

00:16:33.060 --> 00:16:34.360
It's obvious.

00:16:34.360 --> 00:16:37.910
These are the acts of violent, 
inhuman bands of bandits.

00:16:37.910 --> 00:16:41.850
To make it convincing, 
we can't leave witnesses behind.

00:16:42.270 --> 00:16:43.850
How dare you.

00:16:44.270 --> 00:16:47.060
Everything is for the 
prosperity of the empire.

00:16:47.060 --> 00:16:50.230
In the service of a great cause, a few 
small sacrifices are unavoidable.

00:16:50.850 --> 00:16:53.860
And now, you will disappear as well!

00:16:53.860 --> 00:16:55.320
No, we won't.

00:16:55.320 --> 00:16:55.860
What?

00:16:56.570 --> 00:17:00.870
We won't let ourselves be killed 
here by cowards like you!

00:17:01.570 --> 00:17:05.800
We four, the Crimson Vow, 
will return to the capital together!

00:17:06.570 --> 00:17:08.250
It's just as Mile says!

00:17:08.740 --> 00:17:10.710
We can't have you looking down on us.

00:17:11.070 --> 00:17:13.060
We're doing this, Reina-san.

00:17:13.060 --> 00:17:14.220
I know!

00:17:14.480 --> 00:17:16.320
You're spouting nonsense.

00:17:16.320 --> 00:17:18.470
Annihilate them! Don't let them leave alive!

00:17:22.400 --> 00:17:24.140
Godspeed Sword!

00:17:25.620 --> 00:17:27.850
Boiling Water Ball!

00:17:30.520 --> 00:17:32.650
Fireball!

00:17:32.970 --> 00:17:35.440
Fool! That won't work on me!

00:17:35.440 --> 00:17:36.400
Icicle!

00:17:41.880 --> 00:17:43.160
You're the fool!

00:17:43.950 --> 00:17:47.360
We're losing to these little
Hunter girls? What's going on?

00:17:47.360 --> 00:17:49.420
D-Do not falter! Get them!

00:17:51.690 --> 00:17:53.680
Wear away the soles of their shoes at an angle!

00:17:53.680 --> 00:17:55.760
And put some spiky pebbles in them!

00:18:00.480 --> 00:18:02.510
Ow! Ow, ow, ow! Ow!

00:18:02.510 --> 00:18:05.610
Ow, that hurts! What happened?

00:18:05.610 --> 00:18:06.270
Was it magic?

00:18:06.650 --> 00:18:09.130
That's more than enough to take care of you.

00:18:09.130 --> 00:18:12.360
Using nanomachines for 
ridiculous magic like this...

00:18:12.360 --> 00:18:14.230
You're the first, Mile-sama.

00:18:14.990 --> 00:18:16.440
What are you doing?

00:18:16.440 --> 00:18:19.880
You call yourselves proud 
soldiers of the Albarn Empire?

00:18:19.880 --> 00:18:21.980
Will you not fulfill your mission?

00:18:25.520 --> 00:18:26.960
I will not forgive you.

00:18:30.340 --> 00:18:31.340
Fine!

00:18:31.780 --> 00:18:33.560
Go ahead and kill me!

00:18:33.560 --> 00:18:37.090
If I must live the rest of my 
life in shame, I'd rather die!

00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:38.520
Reina-san!

00:18:38.520 --> 00:18:39.270
Mile...

00:18:42.760 --> 00:18:45.100
Blaze brightly, righteous fires of Hell!

00:18:45.630 --> 00:18:48.300
Burn him to ash!

00:18:58.160 --> 00:19:00.910
Who'd bother to kill someone like you?

00:19:05.120 --> 00:19:07.000
Ah! I feel so much better!

00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:27.400
With this, the bandit issue 
has been brought to a close.

00:19:27.400 --> 00:19:31.850
Now, the Kingdom of Tils and the 
Albarn Empire should settle the rest.

00:19:31.850 --> 00:19:35.610
I'm sure the kingdom will avenge its people.

00:19:36.140 --> 00:19:38.240
We can only hope.

00:19:38.240 --> 00:19:38.970
But...

00:19:39.360 --> 00:19:42.280
Her grandfather won't come back.

00:19:46.970 --> 00:19:49.320
Who won't come back?

00:19:49.320 --> 00:19:50.290
You're asking who?

00:19:52.460 --> 00:19:54.080
You mean me?

00:19:54.370 --> 00:19:55.630
Grandfather!

00:19:55.630 --> 00:19:57.460
Old-timer! You're alive?

00:19:57.920 --> 00:19:59.710
How are you here?

00:20:00.360 --> 00:20:01.970
The thing is...

00:20:11.910 --> 00:20:13.880
Greetings, people of Amroth!

00:20:13.880 --> 00:20:15.650
Wh-Who are you?

00:20:15.650 --> 00:20:16.420
Huh?

00:20:24.320 --> 00:20:27.460
It happened in a flash.

00:20:27.460 --> 00:20:31.580
I couldn't move for the terror.

00:20:32.240 --> 00:20:36.410
But I couldn't just hide 
by myself and do nothing.

00:20:36.410 --> 00:20:40.080
I gathered my resolve and decided to fight.

00:20:40.080 --> 00:20:42.070
I was prepared to die there.

00:20:43.010 --> 00:20:44.430
Grandpa!

00:20:45.850 --> 00:20:49.060
As long as there's breath in 
my body, I won't let you die.

00:20:50.670 --> 00:20:53.560
But I couldn't die.

00:20:54.300 --> 00:20:57.720
I ran. I got lost in the forest.

00:20:57.720 --> 00:21:01.070
And I've finally made it back.

00:21:06.700 --> 00:21:07.490
Grandpa?

00:21:10.420 --> 00:21:11.620
Anne!

00:21:11.760 --> 00:21:12.940
Anne!

00:21:12.940 --> 00:21:14.750
Grandpa!

00:21:14.750 --> 00:21:17.750
Grandpa! Grandpa!

00:21:17.930 --> 00:21:22.020
Anne... I'm sorry I scared you.

00:21:22.020 --> 00:21:23.510
There, there.

00:21:23.820 --> 00:21:26.580
Old-timer, I'm glad you made it back alive!

00:21:28.760 --> 00:21:30.820
I-I'm so glad!

00:21:30.820 --> 00:21:34.360
I'm so glad! I'm so happy for you!

00:21:34.880 --> 00:21:37.560
Dear, dear, Mavis. There, there.

00:21:37.980 --> 00:21:41.230
Old-timer, we're gonna expect 
you to keep working hard!

00:21:41.230 --> 00:21:42.760
Huh? But...

00:21:43.130 --> 00:21:47.230
The Crimson Vow have 
captured all the bandits!

00:21:47.230 --> 00:21:49.600
What? Really?

00:21:49.600 --> 00:21:52.180
Thank you, Crimson Vow!

00:21:52.890 --> 00:21:57.580
I really am glad. Anne-chan didn't
 lose any more of her precious family.

00:21:57.860 --> 00:21:59.080
Right, Reina-san?

00:22:00.390 --> 00:22:01.370
Yes.

00:22:03.900 --> 00:22:07.420
All right, Crimson Vow! Back to the capital!

00:22:07.420 --> 00:22:09.160
Yeah!

00:22:09.970 --> 00:22:12.930
Didn't I Say to Make My Abilities 
Average in the Next Life?!
